Braces
******

.[perex]
The `braces` section decides where curly braces go: on which line the opening brace of a class, a function, a closure (an anonymous function) and a control structure stands, where `else` and `catch` go, how an empty body is written, and when braces are required.

Where the `{` goes is the most visible decision of every style, and also the one where styles differ most often. That is why each kind of construct has its own key: a class, a function, a function with parameters on several lines, a closure, an anonymous class and a control structure. PSR-12 and [PER Coding Style 3.1 |https://www.php-fig.org/per/coding-style/] put the brace of a declaration on the next line, and the brace of everything else on the same line as its head:

```neon
braces:
	position:
		class: nextLine
		function: nextLine
		closure: sameLine
		controlStructure: sameLine
		continuingKeyword: sameLine
```

```php .[before]
class Cart {  // Expected a line break before the opening brace.
	public function add(Item $item): void {  // Expected a line break before the opening brace.
		if ($item->isFree())
		{  // Expected no line break before the opening brace.
			return;
		}
		$this->items[] = $item;
	}
}
```

```php .[after]
class Cart
{
	public function add(Item $item): void
	{
		if ($item->isFree()) {
			return;
		}
		$this->items[] = $item;
	}
}
```

Besides the opening brace, DressCode checks that the body after it starts on a new line and that the closing brace stands on a line of its own. The exceptions have their own keys: an empty body `{}`, which `braces.emptyBody` decides separately for a class, a function, a closure, a property hook, an anonymous class and a control structure, and a closure written entirely on one line (`braces.singlelineClosure`). The indentation of the lines this creates belongs to the [indentation |indentation] section, and the blank lines after and before a brace to the [blankLines |blankLines] section.


braces.alternativeSyntax
========================

`if: … endif;` is written with braces.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · covers `no_alternative_syntax` .[decision-facts]


braces.bracelessBody
====================

The body of a control structure written without braces, `if ($a) foo();`.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `forbidden`, psr12 `forbidden`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · covers `control_structure_braces`, `Generic.ControlStructures.InlineControlStructure` .[decision-facts]

```neon
braces:
	bracelessBody: forbidden
```

```php .[before]
if ($item->isFree()) return;  // The body of the `if` must be enclosed in braces.
```

```php .[after]
if ($item->isFree()) {
	return;
}
```


braces.bareStatementGroup
=========================

`{ … }` around statements that nothing opens.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · covers `no_unneeded_braces`, `no_unneeded_curly_braces` .[decision-facts]


braces.position.class
=====================

Where the `{` of a class, an interface, a trait and an enum stands, the members starting a line below it and the `}` taking a line of its own.

- `sameLine`: on the line of what comes before
- `nextLine`: on the next line
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `nextLine`, psr12 `nextLine`, nette `nextLine`, symfony `nextLine`, laravel `nextLine` · covers `braces_position`, `PSR2.Classes.ClassDeclaration` .[decision-facts]

```neon
braces:
	position:
		class: sameLine
```

```php .[before]
class Cart
{  // Expected no line break before the opening brace.
	private array $items = [];
}
```

```php .[after]
class Cart {
	private array $items = [];
}
```


braces.position.function
========================

Where the `{` of a function and of a method whose parameters stand on one line stands, the `{` of a property hook and of the list of hooks staying on the line of its head; the body starts a line below it and the `}` takes a line of its own.

- `sameLine`: on the line of what comes before
- `nextLine`: on the next line
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `nextLine`, psr12 `nextLine`, nette `nextLine`, symfony `nextLine`, laravel `nextLine` · covers `braces_position`, `Squiz.Functions.MultiLineFunctionDeclaration` .[decision-facts]

All the standards put the brace of a function on the next line. If you want it on the same line as the function head, write `sameLine`. A function with parameters on several lines follows the key `braces.position.multilineSignature`.

```neon
braces:
	position:
		function: sameLine
```

```php .[before]
function total(array $items): int
{  // Expected no line break before the opening brace.
	return count($items);
}
```

```php .[after]
function total(array $items): int {
	return count($items);
}
```


braces.position.multilineSignature
==================================

Where the `{` of a function and of a method whose parameters are spread over lines stands.

- `sameLine`: on the line of the `)`
- `nextLine`: on the line below the `)`
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `sameLine`, psr12 `sameLine`, nette `sameLine`, symfony `sameLine`, laravel `sameLine` · covers `braces_position`, `Squiz.Functions.MultiLineFunctionDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


braces.position.typedMultilineSignature
=======================================

Where the `{` of a function and of a method whose parameters are spread over lines stands after a return type; where it is kept, `braces.position.multilineSignature` says it.

- `sameLine`: on the line of the return type
- `nextLine`: on the line below the return type
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `nextLine`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]

Nette Coding Standard uses the value `nextLine`: a function without a return type has `) {` as in PER Coding Style, and for a function with a return type, `): void` stands on a line of its own and the brace goes below it.

```neon
braces:
	position:
		multilineSignature: sameLine
		typedMultilineSignature: nextLine
```

```php .[before]
function send(
	string $to,
	string $subject,
): void {  // Expected a line break before the opening brace.
	mail($to, $subject);
}

function log(
	string $message,
)
{  // Expected no line break before the opening brace.
	echo $message;
}
```

```php .[after]
function send(
	string $to,
	string $subject,
): void
{
	mail($to, $subject);
}

function log(
	string $message,
) {
	echo $message;
}
```


braces.position.closure
=======================

Where the `{` of a closure stands, the body starting a line below it and the `}` taking a line of its own.

- `sameLine`: on the line of what comes before
- `nextLine`: on the next line
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `sameLine`, psr12 `sameLine`, nette `sameLine`, symfony `sameLine`, laravel `sameLine` · covers `braces_position`, `Squiz.Functions.MultiLineFunctionDeclaration` .[decision-facts]

```neon
braces:
	position:
		closure: nextLine
```

```php .[before]
$double = function (int $x) {  // Expected a line break before the opening brace.
	return $x * 2;
};
```

```php .[after]
$double = function (int $x)
{
	return $x * 2;
};
```


braces.position.anonymousClass
==============================

Where the `{` of an anonymous class stands, on the next line always where its interfaces are spread over lines, the members starting a line below it and the `}` taking a line of its own.

- `sameLine`: on the line of what comes before
- `nextLine`: on the next line
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `sameLine`, psr12 `sameLine`, nette `sameLine`, symfony `sameLine`, laravel `nextLine` · covers `braces_position`, `PSR12.Classes.AnonClassDeclaration` .[decision-facts]

```neon
braces:
	position:
		anonymousClass: nextLine
```

```php .[before]
$logger = new class implements Logger {  // Expected a line break before the opening brace.
	public function log(string $message): void
	{
		echo $message;
	}
};
```

```php .[after]
$logger = new class implements Logger
{
	public function log(string $message): void
	{
		echo $message;
	}
};
```


braces.position.controlStructure
================================

Where the `{` of `if`, `else`, a loop, `declare`, `try`, `catch`, `finally`, `switch` and `match` stands, the body starting a line below it and the `}` taking a line of its own.

- `sameLine`: on the line of what comes before
- `nextLine`: on the next line
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `sameLine`, psr12 `sameLine`, nette `sameLine`, symfony `sameLine`, laravel `sameLine` · covers `braces_position`, `PSR12.Files.DeclareStatement`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ControlSignature` .[decision-facts]

```neon
braces:
	position:
		controlStructure: nextLine
```

```php .[before]
if ($ready) {  // Expected a line break before the opening brace.
	start();
}
```

```php .[after]
if ($ready)
{
	start();
}
```


braces.position.continuingKeyword
=================================

Where the keyword continuing a structure after its `}` stands: `else`, `elseif`, `catch`, `finally` and the `while` of `do`.

- `sameLine`: on the line of what comes before
- `nextLine`: on the next line
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `sameLine`, psr12 `sameLine`, nette `sameLine`, symfony `sameLine`, laravel `sameLine` · covers `control_structure_continuation_position`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ControlSignature` .[decision-facts]

```neon
braces:
	position:
		continuingKeyword: sameLine
```

```php .[before]
try {
	connect();
}
catch (ConnectionException $e) {  // Expected no line break before the `catch` keyword.
	retry();
}
```

```php .[after]
try {
	connect();
} catch (ConnectionException $e) {
	retry();
}
```

If your style starts every branch on a new line, use `nextLine`:

```neon
braces:
	position:
		continuingKeyword: nextLine
```

```php .[before]
if ($ready) {
	start();
} else {  // Expected a line break before the `else` keyword.
	wait();
}
```

```php .[after]
if ($ready) {
	start();
}
else {
	wait();
}
```


braces.emptyBody.class
======================

How the empty body of a class, an interface, a trait and an enum is written; a comment inside makes it not empty.

- `collapsed`: `{}` on the line of the head
- `expanded`: `{` and `}` placed as those of any other body
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `collapsed`, psr12 `expanded`, nette `expanded`, symfony `expanded`, laravel `collapsed` · covers `single_line_empty_body` .[decision-facts]

PER Coding Style shortens empty bodies, so the `perCs` preset has the value `collapsed`; PSR-12 and the other standards put each brace on its own line.

```neon
braces:
	emptyBody:
		class: collapsed
		function: collapsed
```

```php .[before]
class NotFound extends Exception
{  // Expected no line break before the opening brace.
}  // Expected no line break before the closing brace.

class Point
{
	public function __construct(private int $x, private int $y)
	{  // Expected no line break before the opening brace.
	}  // Expected no line break before the closing brace.
}
```

```php .[after]
class NotFound extends Exception {}

class Point
{
	public function __construct(private int $x, private int $y) {}
}
```


braces.emptyBody.function
=========================

How the empty body of a function and a method is written; a comment inside makes it not empty.

- `collapsed`: `{}` on the line of the head
- `expanded`: `{` and `}` placed as those of any other body
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `collapsed`, psr12 `expanded`, nette `expanded`, symfony `expanded`, laravel `collapsed` · covers `single_line_empty_body` .[decision-facts]


braces.emptyBody.closure
========================

How the empty body of a closure is written; a comment inside makes it not empty.

- `collapsed`: `{}` on the line of the head
- `expanded`: `{` and `}` placed as those of any other body
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `collapsed`, psr12 `expanded`, nette `expanded`, symfony `expanded`, laravel `collapsed` · covers `single_line_empty_body` .[decision-facts]


braces.emptyBody.propertyHook
=============================

How the empty body of a property hook is written; a comment inside makes it not empty.

- `collapsed`: `{}` on the line of the head
- `expanded`: `{` and `}` placed as those of any other body
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `collapsed`, psr12 `expanded`, nette `expanded`, symfony `expanded`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]


braces.emptyBody.anonymousClass
===============================

How the empty body of an anonymous class is written, one written on one line staying where it is kept; a comment inside makes it not empty.

- `collapsed`: `{}` on the line of the head, one holding a comment staying on its line as written
- `expanded`: `{` and `}` placed as those of any other body
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `collapsed`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `collapsed` · covers `braces_position`, `single_line_empty_body` .[decision-facts]


braces.emptyBody.controlStructure
=================================

How the empty body of an `if`, `else`, a loop, `declare`, `try`, `catch` and `finally` is written; a comment inside makes it not empty.

- `collapsed`: `{}` on the line of the head
- `expanded`: `{` and `}` placed as those of any other body
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]

No standard shortens an empty control structure; `collapsed` is for a project that wants to see a loop without a body on one line. A loop whose body holds a comment is not empty, and it stays as it is.

```neon
braces:
	emptyBody:
		controlStructure: collapsed
```

```php .[before]
while ($reader->next()) {
}  // Expected no line break before the closing brace.
```

```php .[after]
while ($reader->next()) {}
```


braces.singlelineClosure
========================

A closure written whole on one line.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `forbidden`, psr12 `forbidden`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `forbidden` · covers `braces_position` .[decision-facts]

PSR-12 wants the body of every closure on lines of its own, so the `psr12` and `perCs` presets have `forbidden`.

```neon
braces:
	singlelineClosure: forbidden
```

```php .[before]
$ids = array_map(function ($row) { return $row->id; }, $rows);  // Expected a line break after the opening brace. // Expected a line break before the closing brace.
```

```php .[after]
$ids = array_map(function ($row) {
	return $row->id;
}, $rows);
```
